      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIMS",
          "content": "We aimed to analyze genetic polymorphism of estrogen receptor (ESR) 1 and ESR2 in a series of postmenopausal women with Takotsubo syndrome (TS)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "In total, 81 consecutive white women were prospectively enrolled: 22 with TS (TS group; mean age 71.2\u200a±\u200a9.8 years), 22 with acute myocardial infarction (MI group; mean age 73.2\u200a±\u200a8 years), and 37 asymptomatic healthy controls (CTRL group; mean age 69\u200a±\u200a4.2 years). Genotyping of ESR1 -397C>T (rs2234693) and -351A>G (rs9340799) and ESR2 -1839G>T (rs 1271572) and 1082G>A (rs1256049) genetic variants was performed. We estimated the odds ratio (OR) between the genotype of each examined locus with the occurrence of TS or MI."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The risk of experiencing TS was higher for those study participants carrying the T allele at the rs2234693 locus of the ESR1 gene [OR: 2.0, 95% confidence interval (CI): 0.973-4.11, P\u200a=\u200a0.04, TS vs. MI\u200a+\u200aCTRL; OR: 2.79, 95% CI: 1.17-6.64, P\u200a=\u200a0.016, TS vs. MI alone]. Women carrying a T allele at the rs1271572 locus of the ESR2 gene demonstrated an even higher risk (OR: 3.23, 95% CI: 1.55-6.73, P\u200a=\u200a0.0019, TS vs. MI\u200a+\u200aCTRL; OR: 9.13, 95% CI: 2.78-29.9, P\u200a=\u200a0.0001, TS vs. MI alone)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The study reports preliminary findings suggesting a possible link between ESR polymorphisms and the occurrence of TS. Larger studies are needed to confirm our results."
        }
      ]},
